<title>FRANCE: GEC Alsthom wins 365 mln Ffr Argentine contract.</title>
<headline>GEC Alsthom wins 365 mln Ffr Argentine contract.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-British joint venture GEC Alsthom said on Wednesday it has won a 365 million franc ($62.7 million) turn-key contract for a combined-cycle electricity power plant for the Aluminium of Argentina (Aluar) company.</p>
<p>The plant will generate 120 MW and will supply electricity to an extension of an Aluar factory at Puerto Madryn, 1,500 km south of Buenos Aires. The factory will enter service before the end of 1997, GEC Alsthom said in a statement.</p>
<p>GEC Alsthom is a joint venture between Alcatel Alsthom and General Electric Co Plc (GEC).</p>
<p>($ = 5.824 French Francs)</p>
</text>
